  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "1) Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) at 0.650 acc. The RNA-only space is well-characterized: multiprofile > singleprofile, avgpool > transformer, and scvi_n200 > pca_n2000 > scgpt. Image-only resnet50 is very weak (0.208), but we have zero multimodal evidence. 2) This experiment tests whether adding resnet50 image features via concat fusion to the best-known RNA setup (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) provides any complementary signal beyond the RNA modality alone. It is the minimal multimodal extension—only the model setting and image component change, while all RNA-side settings remain at their validated best. 3) With only 3 experiments remaining, this is the highest-information single step: if multimodal helps, we gain a new direction to exploit (e.g., ViT-L or weighted fusion) in the last 3 slots; if it does not, we confirm RNA-only is the ceiling and can spend remaining budget on fine-grained RNA-only refinements. It avoids changing multiple variables at once and directly addresses the largest unexplored design axis."
}

